! mcp_bootstrap_p196.strap -- MCP printed page 196: the whole UNLOAD
! command, from its banner to the card that branches away to K SUPP.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.203.  The header was READ, not
! assumed, at 400 dpi:  "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID LH000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  196".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK. <<<
! Blank paper after the word LOCATION, with only the dashed rule
! running through it; no digits were invented from that rule.  That
! is the rule in docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1 behaving
! exactly as stated: the field is LINE 1'S location and line 1 here
! is an asterisk banner card that compiles nothing.  A blank does
! NOT mean the page has no origin -- the origin is line 4's
! 221733.00.  One more page for that rule, still no counterexample.
!
! >>> AND THE HEADING'S OWN "CARD ID" IS LH000001. <<<  A brand new
! card prefix starting at serial 1, printed on line 1.  Together
! with blank paper below LH000041 that is what says nothing fell off
! either end of this page: there is no LH000000 to have lost.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-EIGHT PRINTED LINES.  Lines 1-3 are the banner
! ("*****  U N L O A D  *****") and compile nothing.  Line 5 is a
! printed "SLC,$" which emits nothing.  THE OTHER FORTY-FOUR ALL
! COMPILE, and the page is CONTIGUOUS from 221733.00 to 221766.37
! -- no reservation, no forward SLC, no hole of any kind -- and then
! blank paper to the foot of the form.
!
!   lines  1-3    the UNLOAD banner.
!   lines  4-14   entry.  K UNLOD loads the "UNLOAD" message
!                 address, tests S MOUNT, sets the message length,
!                 and forks on S OWNER: the owner's path (Z UNLO1)
!                 transmits Z ID16 into Z UNLO2 and falls into
!                 Z UNLO3, the other goes out through the
!                 SIC,Z ID09X / B,Z ID09 name-conversion call.
!   lines 15-26   K F UNLD: pick up the current reel address and the
!                 address of the next reel name, BXVZ to K CUSTM if
!                 a scratch tape is wanted, otherwise K RITE T
!                 expands the reel number (LF(BU,30,6)) and either
!                 branches to K K TAPE or transmits K EX TAP into
!                 K REEL N, stores the expanded number with
!                 SF(BU,40), and calls S A8 IQS with the three-card
!                 argument list VF / CF,5 / VF.
!   lines 27-35   K UNLD1: test the file-protect bit, set the
!                 protect-message length, SV the return, call
!                 K CONV through K CONV R with a VF,0.0 argument,
!                 CNOP to a word boundary, and LX/SX the I-O
!                 instruction address into S IO INS.
!   lines 36-44   K FIRE: issue the UNLOAD control command, take the
!                 reject exit to M IO REJ, wait for end of operation
!                 through K EOP R / K SEOP T, then call the console
!                 message routine S COMM through S COMIC with two
!                 bare-address argument cards.
!   lines 45-48   set the reminder-message time from $TC, store it
!                 in S RMTC, clear S RMIND, and K NEW TP branches
!                 away to K SUPP.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SPAN, ESTABLISHED FROM THE PAGE (NOT FROM THE SURVEY)
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! No survey endpoint was consulted; the brief no longer quotes them.
! Three independent readings of this page agree, and the third is
! arithmetic rather than ink:
!
!   * THE COUNTER CHAIN CLOSES WITH NO SLACK.  Of the forty-four
!     compiling rows, ELEVEN ARE FULL WORDS (lines 6, 8, 13, 18, 20,
!     21, 27, 36, 45, 46, 47 -- each printing TWO half-word groups)
!     and THIRTY-THREE ARE HALF WORDS.  11 + 33/2 = 27.5 words.  The
!     page runs 221733.00 .. 221766.40, which is 0o221766 - 0o221733
!     = 0o33 = 27 words plus one half word = 27.5 words EXACTLY.
!     Every intermediate location is printed and no two of them have
!     a gap.  A lost row would show up as half a word of slack.
!
!   * THE LINE COLUMN runs 1..48 with no break.  Line 48 is located
!     (221766.00); nothing is printed below it but the closing
!     dashed rule and blank paper.
!
!   * THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN runs LH000001 (line 1) to LH000041
!     (line 48) -- FORTY-ONE serials for forty-eight lines, and the
!     heading's own CARD ID agrees with line 1's.  The seven
!     duplicates are all PAIRS OF STATEMENTS PUNCHED ON ONE CARD:
!
!        LH000010  lines 10/11   SIC,ZID09X ; B,ZID09
!        LH000021  lines 22/23   LVI,15,$+1.0 ; B,SA8IQS
!        LH000028  lines 30/31   SIC,KCONVR ; B,KCONV
!        LH000031  lines 34/35   LX,0,$+1.0 ; SX,0,SIOINS($12)
!        LH000033  lines 37/38   LVI,1,$+1.0 ; B,MIOREJ
!        LH000034  lines 39/40   SIC,KEOPR ; B,KSEOPT
!        LH000035  lines 41/42   SIC,SCOMIC ; B,SCOMM
!
!     Every one is a call pair -- four SIC/branch and three
!     LVI-or-LX/branch -- which is the "one card, one WORD" shape
!     printed p.184 recorded and printed p.192 found again.  48 - 7
!     = 41, and the accounting is LINE BY LINE rather than merely
!     consistent: the three banner lines each carry their OWN serial
!     (LH000001, LH000002, LH000003), every other line is either a
!     serial of its own or the second statement of a named pair
!     above, and the run LH000001..LH000041 has no gap in it.
!
! THE SECOND, MACHINE READING (workflow step 2a), MEASURED.
! `python3 strap/mcp_ocr.py 196` reads NINETEEN of the forty-four
! located rows and agrees with the eye on SIXTEEN of them
! (221733.00, 221733.40, 221734.40, 221736.40, 221737.00, 221741.00,
! 221741.40, 221742.00, 221745.40, 221751.00, 221752.40, 221753.40,
! 221754.40, 221755.40, 221761.00, 221761.40).  THREE DISAGREE and
! all three are the OCR dropping or inventing a digit:
!
!   tesseract 221746.46  eye 221746.40 (line 22).  The eye wins and
!             it is not close: 0o46 is not a half-word boundary at
!             all, line 21 is a FULL WORD at 221745.40 so the
!             counter stands at 221746.40, and line 23 prints
!             221747.00 one half word after line 22's half word.
!   tesseract 222175.00  -- six digits that no row on this page
!             carries; the row is out of counter order where it is
!             printed and is simply garbage.
!   tesseract 221756.40  -- NO ROW ON THIS PAGE IS LOCATED AT
!             221756.40 (line 36 is a FULL WORD beginning at
!             221756.00, so .40 is its second half, not a row's
!             location), and the reading is printed between
!             221745.40 and 221751.00 in tesseract's own output;
!             the row in that position on the page is 221750.40.
!
! Recorded in full because a disagreement found and settled is
! worth more than sixteen silent agreements.
!
! The volume OCR of THIS page (docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt, PDF
! p.203 block) is NOT used as a witness anywhere in this deck --
! same ink, worse reader.  The PDF p.204 block, which is printed
! p.197, IS used, and heavily; see THE JOIN.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN, BOTH WAYS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BACKWARD.  >>> NO ORIGIN SLC IS PRINTED ON THIS PAGE. <<<  Line 4
! is simply the first located card, at 221733.00.  (Line 5's printed
! "SLC,$" is NOT the origin -- it stands between line 4's half word
! and line 6 and sets the counter to the 221733.40 it already holds.)
! So this deck writes a hard "SLC,(8)221733.0" that the page does not
! print.
!
! >>> BUT THE ORIGIN IS CHECKED, NOT ASSERTED, AND IT WAS MEASURED.
! <<<  printed p.184's LANDED deck SYNs FOUR labels that THIS page
! defines, every one of them off its own printed binary and all of
! them long before anybody opened p.196:
!
!     KRITET  SYN, (8)221743.0    ! p.184: "p.196 line 18's defining
!                                 !  card reads 221743.00"
!     KUNLD1  SYN, (8)221751.0
!     KFIRE   SYN, (8)221756.0    ! p.184: "printed p.196 line 36
!                                 !  DEFINES it"
!     KNEWTP  SYN, (8)221766.00   ! p.184: "line 18 SIC -- BIT-EXACT"
!
! All four land where p.184 predicted when this deck's origin is
! 221733.00.  The injection the brief asks for was run (merge
! pp.99-192 plus this page, origin shifted one half word to
! (8)221733.40) and the merge REFUSED, naming those symbols.  So
! this is the CHECKED case and not printed p.189's false positive:
! p.184 reaches these labels through SYN values of its own reading,
! and shifting the origin really does break the merge.  The result
! is recorded under JOINING IT TO THE BODY IMAGE.
!
! FORWARD.  >>> THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 221766.40. <<<  Line
! 48 is a half-word branch at 221766.00.  And printed p.197's own
! ink says the same thing from the other side: the volume OCR's PDF
! p.204 block opens
!
!   1*  221766.40  000000.40 8B  221770.74 00  K CUSTM
!                                BZB,S OWNER($11),K KUSTM
!
! -- p.197's LINE 1, located at 221766.40, DEFINING the K CUSTM that
! this page's line 17 branches to.  That is an OCR of a DIFFERENT
! page, which is the one thing the workflow says the volume OCR is
! good for, and it closes the forward join independently of my
! arithmetic.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> FALSIFIABLE PREDICTIONS FOR printed p.197 (PDF p.204) <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   (1) >>> ITS FIRST LOCATED ROW IS 221766.40, AND ITS NAME IS
!       K CUSTM. <<<  Two independent reasons: this page's counter
!       leaves at 221766.40, and this page's line 17 reads K CUSTM
!       at 221766.40 (half word only -- BXVZ is a branch, see the
!       EXTERNALS note).  A first location of 221766.00 or 221767.00
!       falsifies one of them.
!   (2) Its first card serial is LH000042.  WEAKER THAN (1): the
!       brief records two measured cases of a serial printing no
!       listing line at a page break (ED000049, IH000041).  A serial
!       BELOW LH000042 would falsify the join; a missing LH000042
!       would not.
!   (3) Its heading-row LOCATION field is NUMBERED and reads 221766,
!       because its line 1 is a located card and not a banner.  This
!       page is the blank case for the same rule.
!   (4) p.197 DEFINES, at these locations:
!            K K TAPE  221775.00   TI,2,K SCRAC,K REEL N
!            K UNL M   222001.00   an (IQSX)DD(BU,64) message
!            K REEL N  222006.00   an (IQSX)DD(BU) reel number
!            Z UNLO2   222011.00   an (IQSX)DD(BU)
!            K EX TAP  222015.00   an (IQSX)DD(BU,64)
!            K UL MES  222017.40   VF,K UNL M+.192
!       NONE of these is my reading -- they are the volume OCR of
!       p.197, used as an index, and five of the six agree digit for
!       digit with what THIS page's binary requires (see EXTERNALS).
!   (5) p.197 line 3 is "B,K F UNLD+.32" at 221770.00, printing
!       221742.10 00.  That is a reference INTO this page: K F UNLD
!       is line 15 here at 221741.40, and +32 bits is 221742.00.
!       So p.197's deck will check this page's line 15 for free.
!   (6) p.197 lines 12 and 14 reference K UNLD1 (221751.00) and
!       K UNLD1+1.32 (221752.40), both this page's line 27.
!   (7) p.197 defines none of this page's eight labels.
!
! >>> AND ONE BACKWARD, FOR printed p.195 <<<
!   (8) printed p.195's last located row leaves the counter at
!       221733.00 exactly.  This page prints no SLC of its own
!       before line 4, so there is nothing between the two pages.
!       If p.195 ends at 221732.40 with a half word, that is the
!       same statement; if it ends anywhere else, one of us is
!       wrong.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every line number carries the ordinary trailing asterisk.
! THREE ROWS CARRY A SECOND ASTERISK AFTER THE LOCATION:
!
!     line  5   221733.40 *   SLC,$
!     line 22   221746.40 *   LVI,15,$+1.0
!     line 43   221762.00 *   ,0.0($5)
!
! Recorded, and NO RULE PROPOSED.  The brief's count of eight things
! the mark is not stands; this page adds nothing to it and refutes
! nothing, and a rule drawn from one page has been killed the same
! afternoon before (printed p.147 against printed p.151).  What is
! worth saying is only this: line 22 is "LVI,15,$+1.0" and carries
! the mark while line 37's "LVI,1,$+1.0" does not, so on this page
! too the mark is not a function of the statement text.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (0) NO BLANKET "ROUND GLYPH IS A DAMAGED 0" RULE WAS APPLIED.  The
!     brief's measurement stands: neither width nor openness
!     separates O from 0 from C on this drum.  Every round glyph
!     below was settled by another page, by the octal field, or by
!     the compiled word.
!
! (1) THE OCTAL FIELDS DROP INK CONSTANTLY HERE, which is the rung-5
!     calibration and nothing more.  Lines 6, 8, 16, 18, 27, 36, 43
!     and 47 print "COCCOO" or "COCC00" where only 000000 is
!     possible; line 13 prints "222011.C2" and line 18 "036600.C6"
!     and line 29 "221754.C5" and line 35 "COCC04.C1", all in fields
!     that can hold only octal digits.  Per the workflow this
!     licenses nothing about any particular glyph.
!
! (2) "S A8 IQS" (line 23) IS A Q, NOT AN O OR A C.  Three
!     independent reasons and the ink is only the third:
!       * printed p.147's LANDED deck spells it SA8IQS and SYNs it
!         at (8)230566.0, and its line 39 prints the identical half
!         word "230566.10 00" that this page's line 23 prints;
!       * p.147's deck records the CALLING SEQUENCE for it --
!         "LVI,$15,$+1.0 / B,SA8IQS / VF,... / CF,2.0" -- and lines
!         22-26 here are exactly that shape (LVI,15,$+1.0 / B / VF /
!         CF,5 / VF);
!       * rendered at 1600 dpi the glyph has a heavy tail crossing
!         the bowl at the lower right, which neither O nor C has.
!     Recorded in that order on purpose: the corpus settled it
!     before the render did.
!
! (3) "Z ID09X" AND "Z ID09" (lines 10, 11) ARE D-ZERO-NINE, NOT
!     O-O-NINE.  This is the brief's ZID09/ZIO09 hazard and it is
!     settled by the corpus, not by shape: lines 10/11 are THE SAME
!     CARD as printed p.179 lines 47/48, printed p.184 lines 12/13
!     and printed p.166 lines 22/23, all of which print the same two
!     half words (221045.00 80 and 221042.10 00), and printed p.180
!     DEFINES both names.  Four landed decks spell them ZID09X and
!     ZID09 and none spells them with an O.
!
! (4) "Z ID16" (line 13) is the same D.  printed p.180 line 22
!     DEFINES it at 221062.00 as "(IQSX)DD(BU), **MCP**X", and this
!     page's TI prints 221062.00 for it.
!
! (5) THE BYTE ON LINES 7, 9, 14, 22, 28 AND 37 IS "01", NOT "C1".
!     Not a shape call: all six are LVI, whose byte is the bare
!     opcode because the index goes in the 6-bit field as 2J+1 --
!     J=5 gives 0o13, J=7 gives 0o17 twice, J=15 with bit 32 gives
!     0o77, J=7 again 0o17, J=1 gives 0o03.  Every one of those
!     fields is the one this page prints, so the index is accounted
!     for and the byte has nothing left to carry.  printed p.184 and
!     printed p.192 print the same 01 on the same operation.
!
! (6) LINE 34's BYTE IS "10" AND LINE 35's IS "1C", and they are the
!     SAME OPERATION BYTE with and without an index.  LX,0,$+1.0 has
!     no index operand; SX,0,S IO INS($12) is indexed by $12, which
!     is the hexadecimal C.  Settled on what produced them, not on
!     the ink, which prints both round glyphs identically.
!
! (7) "UNLOAD" (line 36) and "SEOP" are read with O's, and the row
!     is not a shape call either: the word UNLOAD is the English of
!     the page's own banner three inches above it, and the control
!     code it compiles is 0o137, which the Reference Manual's 729 IV
!     table gives as "Rewind and Unload".  See THE UNLOAD PROBLEM.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE UNLOAD PROBLEM -- A SUBSTITUTION, LABELLED LOUDLY <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 36 PRINTS:
!
!     221756.00   000000.00 8E  000137.15 00   K FIRE
!                 UNLOAD(SEOP),0.0($14)
!
! THE PRINTED FORM WAS HANDED TO strap_asm FIRST, as rule 2 demands,
! and it was REFUSED:
!
!     UNLOAD(SEOP),0.0($14)  ->  unknown data-description mode 'SEOP'
!     UNLOAD,0.0($14)        ->  unknown mnemonic 'UNLOAD'
!
! -- the same two refusals printed p.165 hit with REW before REW
! landed, and for the same reason: UNLOAD is not in strap_asm's
! IO_FUNCTION_OPS, so "(SEOP)" falls through to the dds parser.
!
! THE DECK THEREFORE WRITES "CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),(8)137." INSTEAD,
! which is printed p.165's own precedent and which compiles the
! printed word EXACTLY -- 000000.00 8E 000137.15 00, verified.  The
! !CHECK below is therefore consistent with the statement beside it
! rather than contradicting it; this is the labelled-substitution
! case and not the let-it-fail case.
!
! >>> AND HERE IS THE THIRD LEG THE BRIEF ASKS FOR, WITH ITS ONE
! >>> WEAKNESS STATED. <<<  The bar strap_asm sets for admitting one
! of C28-6129 Appendix B's I-O function pseudo-ops is three-way:
!
!   leg 1  C28-6129 Appendix B NAMES it.  MEASURED:
!          docs/ocr/C28-6129_STRAP-II_with_update_Apr63.txt lines
!          5734 and 8665 both read "UNLOAD Unload".  SOLID.
!   leg 2  the Reference Manual p.132 729 IV control-code table
!          gives the code.  MEASURED: docs/exchange_and_io.md line
!          627 reads "| 137 | Rewind and Unload (no channel signal
!          on completion) |".  >>> THE NAME IS NOT VERBATIM. <<<
!          Appendix B says "Unload"; the table says "Rewind and
!          Unload".  That is PRECISELY the inexactness the
!          IO_FUNCTION_OPS comment flags when it refuses
!          "Backspace" against "Backspace Block", and REW was
!          admitted partly BECAUSE its name matched verbatim.
!   leg 3  a listing that PRINTS the code.  MEASURED: this page,
!          line 36, prints 000137 with .15 = CTLSEOP in bits
!          50-55, exactly the shape printed p.165 printed for REW
!          and printed p.192 for CTL(SEOP).  SOLID.
!
! So two legs are solid and the middle one is near-but-not-verbatim.
! That is a decision about strap/opcodes, which this deck may not
! make and does not pretend to; it is reported instead.  Note also
! that docs/exchange_and_io.md line 633 already says "the model
! implements 136/137 and 176 only", so 0o137 is a code the hardware
! model decodes today -- only the MNEMONIC is missing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWENTY-FIVE.  EIGHTEEN ARE ALREADY LANDED in decks/ and are
! written exactly as the landed decks spell them -- including their
! DATA DESCRIPTIONS and their DECIMAL bit offsets -- so the merged
! image cannot disagree.  Six of them carry a dds and those dds are
! LOAD-BEARING on this page: the ST on line 46 and the CM0000 on
! line 47 write no dds of their own and take their LENGTH from the
! symbol, so "SRMTC SYN(BU,26), 1.32" is what makes line 46 print
! 032000 and "SRMIND SYN(BU,1), 1.63" is what makes line 47 print
! 001000.  Strip either dds and the row compiles with length 0.
!
!   KULMES   222017.40    landed p.184
!   SMOUNT   (BU,1) 0.51  landed, 11 decks; p.99 line 42 defines it
!   KUNLM    222001.0     landed p.184
!   SOWNER   (BU,1) 0.32  landed, 12 decks; p.99 line 30 defines it
!   ZUNLO2   222011.0     landed p.184
!   ZID09X   221045.00    landed pp.166/179/184; p.180 defines it
!   ZID09    221042.0     landed pp.166/179/184; p.180 defines it
!   SCREEL   (BU,18) 8.32 landed, 9 decks; p.101 line 28 defines it
!   KEXTAP   222015.0     landed p.179
!   SA8IQS   230566.0     landed p.147
!   KCONVR   221350.0     landed pp.146/179/180/186
!   KCONV    221335.0     landed pp.146/179/186
!   SIOINS   (BU,64) 4.0  landed, 20 decks; p.101 line 17 defines it
!   MIOREJ   221261.0     landed, 13 decks
!   KEOPR    221354.40    landed, 6 decks
!   KSEOPT   221350.40    landed, 12 decks
!   SCOMIC   215470.40    landed pp.116/131/135/179/186
!   SCOMM    215470.0     landed pp.116/131/135/179/186
!   SRMTC    (BU,26) 1.32 landed pp.101/179; p.101 line 27 defines it
!   SRMIND   (BU,1) 1.63  landed pp.101/179; p.101 line 30 defines it
!   KSUPP    216242.0     landed, 37 decks; p.128 defines it
!
! (That list is twenty-one; three of the twenty-five below are new.)
!
! THREE ARE NEW HERE.  Every value is read off THIS page's own
! BINARY OUTPUT, and every one of the three is ALSO carried by the
! volume OCR of printed p.197 -- a DIFFERENT page, which is the one
! use the workflow allows the volume OCR:
!
! >>> BIT-EXACT FROM THIS PAGE <<<
!   KREELN   222006.00   lines 24 and 26 are "VF,K REEL N+.72", and
!                        a VF DEPOSITS THE VALUE, so the printed
!                        "222007.10+" is a reading of every bit:
!                        222007.08 minus 72 decimal bits is
!                        222006.00 exactly.  (.72 is BARE, so it is
!                        DECIMAL -- the workflow's rule; read as
!                        octal it gives 222006.16 and the row fails.)
!                        Line 21's SF(BU,40) is a VFL operand and
!                        prints the same 222007.10, a second
!                        bit-exact reading of the same symbol.
!                        p.197's OCR line 20 DEFINES "KREELN" at
!                        222006.00, which agrees digit for digit.
!
! >>> HALF WORD ONLY (the bit within the half word is UNOBSERVABLE,
! >>> workflow item 1) <<<
!   KCUSTM   221766.40   line 17 BXVZ -- prints 221766.71, and the
!                        sweep that settled it shows why this is
!                        only the half word:
!                           KCUSTM = (8)221766.0  -> 221766.31 42
!                           KCUSTM = (8)221766.40 -> 221766.71 42
!                        bit 32 shows and nothing below it does.
!                        The .40 is READ (it is not the convention
!                        ".0"), and p.197's OCR line 1 DEFINES
!                        K CUSTM at 221766.40, which is also exactly
!                        where this page's counter stops.
!   KKTAPE   221775.0    line 19 BRZ -- prints 221775.34, and 0o34
!                        is the BRZ code, not address bits.  p.197's
!                        OCR line 11 DEFINES "K K TAPE" at
!                        221775.00, so the bit really is 0; the deck
!                        still writes ".0" because a later page's
!                        RENDERING must replace an OCR and not be
!                        replaced by it.
!
! ONE MORE, AND IT IS NOT A SYMBOL OF THIS DECK: Z ID16, which this
! page's line 13 transmits.  printed p.180 DEFINES it at 221062.00
! with a mode-only "(BU)" data description on an (IQSX)DD card.  The
! stand-in here is written WITHOUT a dds, per the brief's printed
! p.189 rule -- this page witnesses no length for it (TI is
! word-granular and the row compiles identically with and without
! one), so writing "(BU)" would be asserting a length this page
! cannot see.  The merge was run with the bare form and ACCEPTED it.
!
! >>> AND NOTE WHAT THE SIC ROWS BUY. <<<  Four externals are read
! by a SIC on this page and a SIC carries its operand's full 24-bit
! bit address, so those four rows CHECK the landed values rather
! than merely agreeing with them:
!     ZID09X  221045.00 (line 10)   KCONVR  221350.00 (line 30)
!     KEOPR   221354.40 (line 39)   SCOMIC  215470.40 (line 41)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT strap_asm DID AND DID NOT ACCEPT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> A BLANK OPERATION FIELD ASSEMBLES -- AND IT IS ALREADY
! >>> IMPLEMENTED ON PURPOSE, WHICH IS NOT WHAT I FIRST WROTE HERE.
! <<<  Lines 43 and 44 print NO mnemonic at all -- the statement
! field begins with the comma:
!
!     221762.00 *  000000.00 85    ,0.0($5)
!     221762.40    000000.00 87    ,0.0($7)
!
! Handed to strap_asm in exactly that form, both compile, and both
! compile the printed half word.  AN EARLIER DRAFT OF THIS NOTE
! CLAIMED THIS WAS AN UNDOCUMENTED CAPABILITY; it is not.
! strap_asm.py's `op == ''` branch (statement_size and
! emit_statement) carries the primary source already --
! C22-6531 printed p.7: "A MAJOR FIELD MAY BE NULL, even though
! other non-null fields follow it ... if nothing but the comma
! denoting the field termination is written" -- and emits "the
! address-and-index half word every full-word format begins with"
! (Reference Manual printed p.163).  So the right record is that
! THIS PAGE EXERCISES a documented path twice, with the printed
! bytes 85 and 87 confirming the 0b1000 nibble and the index.
! Recorded this way because a claim about the REPO is cheap for the
! caller to check and mine was wrong before I checked it.
!
! REFUSED: "UNLOAD(SEOP),0.0($14)" and "UNLOAD,0.0($14)".  See THE
! UNLOAD PROBLEM.  That is the only refusal on this page.
!
! NAME-FIELD BLANKS.  The page prints its names with blanks -- "K
! UNLOD", "Z UNLO1", "Z UNLO3", "K F UNLD", "K RITE T", "K UNLD1",
! "K FIRE", "K NEW TP" -- and strap_asm cannot carry a blank in a
! LABEL field at all.  They are written closed up, which is also how
! every landed deck writes them and how printed p.184 already SYNs
! four of them.  The printed spellings are in the listing block
! below.  This is printed p.192's open note (8) again and it still
! settles nothing about STRAP's own name field.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT I COULD NOT SETTLE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (A) >>> WHETHER UNLOAD MAY BE ADMITTED AS A MNEMONIC. <<<  Two of
!     the three legs are solid and the middle one is "Rewind and
!     Unload" against Appendix B's "Unload" -- near, but not the
!     verbatim match that admitted REW and not the verbatim
!     mismatch that still excludes BS.  This page cannot decide it
!     and did not try; the substitution is labelled at every
!     occurrence.  WHAT WOULD SETTLE IT: another MCP page printing
!     a DIFFERENT control code against the UNLOAD mnemonic (which
!     would refute 0o137), or a typeset source that spells the 729
!     IV's 137 as plain "Unload".
!
! (B) >>> THE BIT WITHIN THE HALF WORD, for the TEN externals
!     read off a BRANCH or an INDEX operation. <<<  KCUSTM,
!     KKTAPE, ZID09, SA8IQS, KCONV, MIOREJ, KSEOPT, SCOMM, KSUPP
!     and KULMES are each pinned only to bit 32 by this page
!     (workflow item 1).  Six of them are landed at the values
!     written here and two more are carried by printed p.197's
!     OCR, so nothing is unknown -- but nothing on THIS page reads
!     those bits and the deck does not pretend otherwise.  Note
!     which ones ARE bit-exact and why: the four SIC rows
!     (ZID09X, KCONVR, KEOPR, SCOMIC), the three VFL/VF rows for
!     KREELN, the CM1111 for SMOUNT, the BB for SOWNER, and the
!     L/ST/CM0000 trio for $TC, SRMTC and SRMIND.
!
! (C) >>> THE THREE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISKS. <<<  Lines 5, 22 and
!     43.  Recorded, unexplained, NO RULE PROPOSED -- see LISTING
!     MARKS.  A tempting shape here is "the card that opens a
!     call pair", and this page KILLS it from its own ink: line 22
!     opens the LVI/B pair on card LH000021 and carries the mark,
!     while lines 10, 30, 37, 39 and 41 all open the same kind of
!     pair and carry none.
!
! (D) >>> THE BACKWARD JOIN IS UNVERIFIED. <<<  printed p.195 has
!     not been rendered here.  This page's origin is CHECKED by the
!     merge against printed p.184's SYNs, which is a strong but
!     DIFFERENT statement from "p.195 ends at 221733.00".  The
!     latter is prediction (8) and belongs to p.195's transcriber.
!
! (E) >>> LINES 43/44 ARE READ AS NULL-OPERATION CARDS AND I CANNOT
!     PROVE THE DRUM DID NOT SIMPLY DROP A MNEMONIC. <<<  What
!     argues for the reading: two such cards in a row, both
!     compiling the printed half word exactly from the null-
!     operation path, both sitting where a called routine's
!     argument list belongs (immediately after SIC,S COMIC /
!     B,S COMM), and the same shape appearing on lines 24-26 for
!     the S A8 IQS call.  What would settle it: another page
!     printing the same two cards, or a console-message calling
!     sequence in C22-6728 that shows two bare address arguments.
!
! (F) The dds on Z ID16.  printed p.180 defines it with a mode-only
!     "(BU)" and this page witnesses no length for it, so the
!     stand-in here is dds-less (printed p.189's rule).  The merge
!     accepts that today.  Whether a mode-only dds should be
!     carried onto a stand-in is the brief's still-OPEN question
!     and this page does not settle it either: TI is word-granular,
!     so the row compiles identically both ways, which is exactly
!     the shape that CANNOT settle it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! JOINING IT TO THE BODY IMAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS DECK DOES NOT JOIN IT, because pp.193, 194 and 195 are being
! transcribed in parallel and tests/check_mcp_body_image.py's
! FIRST, LAST is 99, 192.  When all of pp.193-200 have landed, LAST
! moves to 200 there -- NOT strap/mcp_image.py's MCP_IPL_PAGES,
! which is the other assembly.
!
! THE MERGE WAS RUN ANYWAY, out of a scratchpad script that calls
! mcp_image.build on pp.99-192 plus this page, and the result is the
! origin check above:
!
!     as written            -> ACCEPTED
!     origin (8)221733.40   -> REFUSED, on KRITET / KUNLD1 /
!                              KFIRE / KNEWTP
!
! so this page's origin is CHECKED and not asserted.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ---------------- externals, landed values first ----------------
KULMES  SYN, (8)222017.40            ! landed p.184; p.197 line 26 defines it
SMOUNT  SYN(BU,1), 0.51              ! landed; p.99 line 42 -MOUNT TAPE
